ExLlamaV3-style FP16 prefill staging (unpack W_f16 once + cuBLASLt FP32-acc GEMM + strided rotOut)

For dense 4- and 6-bit mul1 EXL3 projections on prefill chunks (m >= 256), unpacks
`W_q` ONCE per chunk into row-major FP16 (`tf_exl3_unpack_f16_nk_{12,8}_2`), rotates
inputs to FP16 (`tf_exl3_rot_in`), runs NVIDIA cuBLASLt FP16->FP32 GEMM (`cublaslt.Linear`),
and applies `tf_exl3_rot_out` (`FWHT128 * HAD_SCALE * svh + bias` in FP32) writing directly
into strided output columns (`y_stride = g.n`, eliminating `copyCols` on prefill too).
Gated by `TF_EXL3_PREFILL_CUBLAS` (default 1; `0` restores `exl3_linear_wc`).

Verified on GB10 (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next EXL3 4.05bpw + DFlash2 + MXFP8 KV):
- Cold prefill 4K / 16K / 65K / 248K:
  1,968 / 2,003 / 2,044 / 1,951 -> 2,064 / 2,123 / 2,086 / 2,067 tok/s
  (248K TTFT 126.95 s -> 119.78 s, -7.17 s / +6.0%; cumulative -110.0 s vs pre-Wave-1 229.7 s!)
- Exactness: 120K needle byte-identical to BF16 (sha ae38468a7f52, FALCON-9472-OMEGA),
  4K long prompt byte-identical to BF16 stock (sha 3ac5af9f7e45), 4/4 greedy & T=0.7
  drafts on == drafts off exact.

